## 2. CONTROL: synthetic 5m source stamps through tools/i6e_price_metrics.py:hourly_close (no market data)
normal summer week, source opens 17:00 NY: first source stamp 2024-06-09 17:00 (naive, read as America/New_York BAR_START) -> hourly END labels ['Sun 2024-06-09 22:00 UTC', 'Sun 2024-06-09 23:00 UTC']
DST-start Sunday, US-DST source opens 17:00 EDT: first source stamp 2024-03-10 17:00 (naive, read as America/New_York BAR_START) -> hourly END labels ['Sun 2024-03-10 22:00 UTC', 'Sun 2024-03-10 23:00 UTC']
DST-start Sunday, EU-DST-dated source stamps the same instant as 16:00: first source stamp 2024-03-10 16:00 (naive, read as America/New_York BAR_START) -> hourly END labels ['Sun 2024-03-10 21:00 UTC', 'Sun 2024-03-10 22:00 UTC']
normal winter week, source opens 17:00 NY: first source stamp 2024-01-07 17:00 (naive, read as America/New_York BAR_START) -> hourly END labels ['Sun 2024-01-07 23:00 UTC', 'Mon 2024-01-08 00:00 UTC']
